comment_char %
escape_char /
% Stand-in for glibc's locales/zh_CN: ASCII character classes and a default collation.
% How bytes are decoded depends on the charmap given to localedef.
LC_CTYPE
upper <U0041>..<U005A>
lower <U0061>..<U007A>
digit <U0030>..<U0039>
xdigit <U0030>..<U0039>;<U0041>..<U0046>;<U0061>..<U0066>
space <U0009>..<U000D>;<U0020>
blank <U0009>;<U0020>
cntrl <U0000>..<U001F>;<U007F>
punct <U0021>..<U002F>;<U003A>..<U0040>;<U005B>..<U0060>;<U007B>..<U007E>
END LC_CTYPE
LC_COLLATE
order_start forward
UNDEFINED
order_end
END LC_COLLATE
